[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68266,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Enteric-type adenocarcinoma is a primary thymic neoplasm having the same histological and immunohistochemical features as colorectal adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68267,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8144/3 Adenocarcinoma, enteric-type</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68268,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C27.0 &amp; XH0349 Carcinoma of thymus &amp; Adenocarcinoma, intestinal type</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68269,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> intestinal-type adenocarcinoma; mucinous (colloid) adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68270,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68271,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "<p>Enteric-type adenocarcinoma of the thymus is localized in the anterior (prevascular) mediastinum.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-04T11:39:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68272,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Some patients have chest pain, cough, and dyspnoea {28038793; 18722686}; others are asymptomatic {25517960}. CEA serum levels may be elevated {18722686}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68273,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "<p>Enteric-type adenocarcinomas account for &lt;&nbsp;5% of all thymic carcinomas {29339175}. The average age is 45&nbsp;years, with male predominance {29339175}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T17:11:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68274,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68275,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>An origin from the glandular structures of involuted thymus {12502935} or derivation from thymic cysts has been suggested in selected cases {18722686}. Single cases show mutations of <em>KRAS</em>, <em>TP53</em>, <em>TGFB2</em>, <em>TNFSF15</em>, and <em>MYC</em> and losses of HLA loci at 6p21.32 {28932588; 28506304; 23725376}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68276,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are large, solid or solid-cystic, and at times ill defined, with white to yellowish-white cut surfaces and variable mucin (colloid) content. Most cases are associated with thymic cysts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68277,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour exhibits a mucinous and/or papillotubular morphology or small tumour cell clusters floating in pools of extracellular mucin. Intracellular mucin can occur. Expression of at least one marker of enteric differentiation (CK20, CDX2, MUC2) {28038793} is mandatory. Expression of CK7 and CD5 is variable {25517960}; TTF1 and KIT (CD117) are negative {18722686; 25517960}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68278,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In smears, tumour cells show nuclear crowding and form clusters within extracellular mucin {28772352}. Immunostaining for enteric markers may help to confirm the diagnosis {28038793; 28888068}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68279,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68280,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A primary thymic tumour mimicking colorectal adenocarcinoma</li>\r\n<li>Exclusion of metastasis from an enteric primary</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Expression of at least one marker of enteric differentiation (CK20, CDX2, MUC2)</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-22T16:59:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68281,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "<p>Enteric-type adenocarcinomas should be staged according to the TNM system [[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]] {25396314} and, optionally, the Masaoka&ndash;Koga system {21847052}. Most tumours are in Masaoka&ndash;Koga stages&nbsp;III and IV {28038793}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-14T11:04:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68282,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 241,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In a recent series, 2&nbsp;of 9&nbsp;patients died of the tumour; all others were alive with disease {28038793}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-10-27T10:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]